// AiXenix Cosmos Lab: the bilingual RU/EN handbook (content-owned).
//
// Rendering: the UI (lead) renders Chapter.blocks in order. Every block type is listed in `Block`. A `feature` block shows the
// live status of a tool from FEATURE_STATUS, so the handbook never claims a tool the browser does not have: when a feature is
// wired, its entry in FEATURE_STATUS changes from 'planned' to 'available' (one place), and every chapter follows.
// Search: searchHandbook(query, lang). Glossary: GLOSSARY. Questions: FAQ. Controls: CONTROLS (from the lead's bindings;
// confirmed: false would render a binding as "proposed").
//
// Facts about data come from web/public/data (the exact native catalogue). Physics statements describe the model the data was
// prepared for (Newtonian point masses, SI units); what the browser engine actually integrates is a feature status.

